From 427b864e17d8741efd98b6114085b69bddae4a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Gasper <jmgasper@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:39:54 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 9pfs: Haiku host support

virtio-9p (virtfs) on a Haiku host, as on FreeBSD and macOS:

- xattrs are BFS attributes named "linux:<name>" (raw data), so they do
  not mix with Haiku's own; files without attributes report ENOTSUP;
- statfs from fstatvfs; device numbers in glibc's layout (Haiku's dev_t
  has no major and minor);
- Haiku's dirent has no d_off or d_type: readdir keeps telldir() in the
  unused d_pino and reports DT_UNKNOWN;
- errno values are translated to Linux's, Haiku's B_* codes included;
- mknod makes FIFOs with mkfifoat and sockets by binding a Unix socket
  under a short temporary name and moving it into place (bind takes a
  path of at most 104 bytes); device nodes cannot exist on BFS;
- no O_PATH: chmod of a special file uses fchmodat(AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW),
  and F_SETFL keeps to the flags it can change (the root file system has
  no F_SETFL for directories at all).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
